      },
      "lineNbr": 572,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-21T23:21:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we add a TODO(bug) to remove this? I guess we\u0027ll have to add support in CrOS `libec` for the async frame command.\n\nOr could this synchronous version call the new v1 command and poll for it to be finished? If so, I would add that in a separate CL.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 572,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 572,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "7a5680c1699c501340ecad0a7576914181d3c844",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7118dd2c_62b3575f",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 572,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-29T17:59:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Or could this synchronous version call the new v1 command and poll for it to be finished?\n\nThis sounds really cool, because we could remove duplicated code. I\u0027m afraid about one thing - the HOSTCMD task will wait for result in FP_FRAME host command context. It means that we need to:\n- Sleep in the host command to give CPU to FPSENSOR task\n- Or use semaphores (in Zephyr).\n- Or wakeup HOSTCMD when the work is done (I don\u0027t think EC supports semaphores).\n\nSleeping does not sound that bad, but I would like to hear your opinion about that.",
      "parentUuid": "802e148c_e00df921",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 572,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 572,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "7a5680c1699c501340ecad0a7576914181d3c844",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0713da92_e53cc4ba",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 572,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-29T21:44:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think sleeping is ok as long as it doesn\u0027t break any of the assumptions we made about concurrency.",
      "parentUuid": "7118dd2c_62b3575f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 572,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 572,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "7a5680c1699c501340ecad0a7576914181d3c844",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "26cab913_c6b51406",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 572,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-30T15:19:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried to implement it and found that FP_FRAME_V0 calling FP_FRAME_V1 is very similar to what we have now. We still need to prepare `struct ec_params_fp_frame_v1` which means that we have to check index + it introduces risks mentioned earlier. I think `get_frame()` and `encrypt_template()` functions introduced in parent CL deduplicate code in a reasonable way.\n\nThe code would look more/less like this\n```\nstatic enum ec_status fp_command_frame_v0(struct host_cmd_handler_args *args)\n{\n        /* Copy params */\n        const struct ec_params_fp_frame params_v0 \u003d\n                *static_cast\u003cconst struct ec_params_fp_frame *\u003e(args-\u003eparams);\n\n        auto *params \u003d\n                static_cast\u003cstruct ec_params_fp_frame_v1 *\u003e(args-\u003eparams);\n        params-\u003eoffset \u003d params_v0.offset \u0026 FP_FRAME_OFFSET_MASK;\n        params-\u003esize \u003d params_v0.size;\n        uint16_t idx \u003d FP_FRAME_GET_BUFFER_INDEX(params_v0.offset);\n        enum ec_status status \u003d EC_RES_SUCCESS;\n\n        if (idx \u003d\u003d FP_FRAME_INDEX_RAW_IMAGE) {\n                /* The host requested a frame. */\n                params-\u003ecmd \u003d FP_FRAME_GET_RAW_IMAGE;\n                return fp_command_frame_v1(args);\n        }\n\n        /* The host requested a template. */\n\n        /* Templates are numbered from 1 in this host request. */\n        params-\u003eindex \u003d idx - FP_FRAME_INDEX_TEMPLATE;\n\n        if (!params-\u003eoffset) {\n                /* Host has requested the first chunk, do the encryption. */\n                params-\u003ecmd \u003d FP_FRAME_ENCRYPT_TEMPLATE;\n                status \u003d fp_command_frame_v1(args);\n                if (status !\u003d EC_RES_SUCCESS) {\n                        return status;\n                }\n\n                crec_msleep(10);\n        }\n        params-\u003ecmd \u003d FP_FRAME_GET_ENCRYPTED_TEMPLATE;\n        for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c 20; i++) {\n                status \u003d fp_command_frame_v1(args);\n                if (status !\u003d EC_RES_BUSY) {\n                        break;\n                }\n                crec_msleep(10);\n        }\n\n        return status;\n}\n```\n\nAdded TODO to remove this after migration is completed.",
      "parentUuid": "0713da92_e53cc4ba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 572,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 572,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "7a5680c1699c501340ecad0a7576914181d3c844",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0bf6e52_2450d1e4",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 630,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-21T23:21:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In CrOS `libec`, I tried to create a [standard \"async\" command pattern](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform2/libec/ec_command_async.h).\n\nExamples:\n\n* https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform2/libec/add_entropy_command.cc\n* https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform2/libec/fingerprint/fp_context_command.cc;l\u003d57;drc\u003daf8f850e622dc4ffded892bf5fbcd18fffddb5fd\n\nWould it work to use that same style here for consistency?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 630,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 630,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "7a5680c1699c501340ecad0a7576914181d3c844",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40cfe165_66808235",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 630,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-29T17:59:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How do you think the FP_FRAME could fit in the \"async\" pattern? Do you want me to split FP_FRAME into more separate host commands?\n\nWe are calling \"GET_RESULT\" multiple times. There is also command to get raw image which returns immediately.",
      "parentUuid": "b0bf6e52_2450d1e4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 630,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 630,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "7a5680c1699c501340ecad0a7576914181d3c844",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5e404817_26483f4f",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 630,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-29T21:44:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it work if we split the command into `FP_FRAME` and `FP_FRAME_RAW`, each of which are using the \"async\" pattern?\n\nI don\u0027t want to make this unnecessarily complicated just to fit the \"async\" pattern though, so let me know your thoughts, especially if it will cause more side effects. On the other hand, it doesn\u0027t seem too bad to keep the \"dangerous\" command (`FP_FRAME_RAW`) separate from the normal \"safe\" command. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "40cfe165_66808235",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 630,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 630,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "7a5680c1699c501340ecad0a7576914181d3c844",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b42b52ed_f10ab43d",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 630,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-30T15:19:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Would it work if we split the command into FP_FRAME and FP_FRAME_RAW, each of which are using the \"async\" pattern?\n\nNo. The problem is not in supporting raw frame and template in one command (we would just need to set `action` appropriately), but in downloading the result.\n\nThe \"async\" pattern calls \"GET_RESULT\" action only once, while we need to call it multiple times to download the template.\n\nWe would need to have command for starting encryption and command for downloading result, but in this case neither command would need to be \"async\".",
      "parentUuid": "5e404817_26483f4f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 630,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 630,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "7a5680c1699c501340ecad0a7576914181d3c844",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
